      "source_url": "https://thaqalayn.net/hadith/34/3/31/4",
      "text": [
        ": \"إِنَّ اَللَّهَ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ كَتَبَ عَلَى اَلرِّجَالِ اَلْجِهَادَ وَ عَلَى اَلنِّسَاءِ اَلْجِهَادَ فَجِهَادُ اَلرَّجُلِ أَنْ يَبْذُلَ مَالَهُ وَ دَمَهُ حَتَّى يُقْتَلَ فِي سَبِيلِ اَللَّهِ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ وَ جِهَادُ اَلْمَرْأَةِ أَنْ تَصْبِرَ عَلَى مَا تَرَى مِنْ أَذَى زَوْجِهَا وَ غَيْرَتِهِ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.4516 - Muhammad ibn al-Fudhayl narrated from Shurayh al-Wabishi, from Jabir, from Abu Jafar Imam Muhammad ibn Ali Al-Baqir (as), who said:\n\"Indeed, Allah (swt), the Mighty and Majestic, has ordained jihad upon men and jihad upon women. The jihad of a man is to spend his wealth and sacrifice his blood until he is killed in the way of Allah (swt), the Mighty and Majestic. And the jihad of a woman is to be patient with what she faces from the harm and jealousy of her husband.\""
        ]
      }
    },
